==English==
{{was wotd|2017|October|14}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*(s)ker- (cut)}}
From {{der|en|fro|scrupule}}, from {{der|en|la|scrūpulus||(''literally'') a small [[sharp#Adjective|sharp]] or [[pointed#Adjective|pointed]] [[stone#Noun|stone]]; the [[twenty-fourth]] part of an [[ounce]]; [[uneasiness]] of [[mind#Noun|mind]], [[anxiety]], [[doubt#Noun|doubt]], [[trouble#Noun|trouble]]; scruple}}, [[Appendix:Glossary#diminutive|diminutive]] of {{m|la|scrūpus||a [[rough#Adjective|rough]] or sharp stone; anxiety, uneasiness}}; perhaps akin to {{der|en|grc|σκύρος||the [[chipping#Noun|chippings]] of stone}}, from {{m|grc|ξυρόν||[[razor#Noun|razor]]}}, from {{m|grc|ξύω||to [[scrape#Verb|scrape]]}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ksunyo-}}.

